# Rust Backend Conventions

## Stack

- Actix-web for HTTP, Tokio async runtime
- Serde for serialization, reqwest for HTTP clients
- Supabase (Postgres) for persistence, in-memory cache for hot data

## Structure

- `src/main.rs` — server bootstrap and scheduler
- `src/api/routes.rs` — REST endpoints under `/api/v2/`
- `src/ingestion/` — platform pollers (Kalshi, Polymarket, Culture, Dome)
- `src/processing/arb_detector.rs` — arbitrage detection logic
- `src/storage/` — Supabase client and in-memory cache
- `src/models/` — shared data types (Event, Platform enums)

## API Design

- All responses are JSON, snake_case fields
- Prices are floats 0.0-1.0 (frontend converts to cents)
- Events have `kalshi` and `polymarket` platform odds blocks with `outcomes: Record<string, { yes_price, no_price }>`
